romanized_response:
HTTP status code 429 Too Many Requests andre server nalli yavudo rate limit ide mattu nimma request adannu meeride anta artha. Idu ee kelagina yava karanagalinda aagirabahudu:

1. Ee request maduva code annu kadime samayadalli tumba sala run madirabahudu, aadudinda rate limit exceed aagirabahudu.

2. Website ge spam anta anisuva requests annu adu 429 status code jothe reject maduttade. Idara artha user agent common browser agirade irabahudu; kelavu websites balasuva simple check idu. Idannu sari madalu, GET request ge "User-Agent" header annu ee reethi add madabahudu:

```
const response = await axios.get('https://www.realestate.com.au/rent/in-sydney,+nsw/list-1', 
     { headers: { 'User-Agent': 'browser.version' }  }
);
```

Note: neevu `"browser.version"` annu nijavada browser user agent string inda replace madabeku. Ee code yava application nalli run aguttide annodara mele depend aagi, idannu user agent spoofing anta pariganisabahudu. Kelavu deshagalu athava organizations na laws adannu restrict madabahudu (athava ee code access madalu prayatnisuttiruva website na terms of service kooda restrict madabahudu).

3. Website bere yavudo karanadinda requests ge rate limit maduttirabahudu. Idu request proxy moolaka maduttiruvudarinda agirabahudu; aa sandarbhadalli proxy ya itara users tumba requests madirabahudu, adare idu ashtu sadhyate illa.

4. Website denial of service attack adiyalli iruvudarinda ella requests annu reject maduttirabahudu. Idu sadhyate kadime, yakendre anthaha attack adiyalli server na typical behavior traffic annu non-existent server ge route maduvudu, athava sampoornavagi deny maduvudu, yava valid response kooda kodade iruvudu. Aadaru, website HTTP status code jothe respond madidaroo, server overload aagiddaga koduva server error 503 Service Unavailable agiruva sadhyate hechu.

response_en:
Yes, certainly! The issue you're encountering is because the string literals "fizzbuzz", "fizz", and "buzz" are temporary values, and you are trying to return a reference to them, which is not allowed because they will be dropped at the end of the scope, and the returned reference would be dangling.

You can fix this error by returning &'static str instead of &str. &'static str refers to string literals, which have a 'static lifetime, meaning they last for the duration of the program. Here's an updated version of your code:

fn fizzbuzz(n: usize) -> &'static str {
    match (n % 3, n % 5) {
        (0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",
        (0, _) => "fizz",
        (_, 0) => "buzz",
        _ => {
            let s = n.to_string();
            Box::leak(s.into_boxed_str())
        }
    }
}

Note that the last arm returns a &'static str that is created from a String using the Box::leak function, which takes ownership of a Box<T> and returns a pointer to its contents, effectively leaking it. This is safe because the returned pointer will last for the duration of the program, but it should be used with care as it will not be cleaned up automatically.

romanized_response:
Howdu, kandita! Neevu encounter maaduttiruva issue yendare string literals "fizzbuzz", "fizz", matthu "buzz" temporary values aagive, matthu neevu avugalige reference return maadalu try maaduttiddira. Adu allow agolla, yakendre scope mugida mele avu drop aaguttave, matthu return maadida reference dangling aaguttade.

Ee error annu fix maadalu, &str badalige &'static str return maadabahudu. &'static str andre string literals ge refer maaduttade, avugalige 'static lifetime iruttade, andare program na duration poorthi avu iruttave. Nimma code na updated version illide:

fn fizzbuzz(n: usize) -> &'static str {
    match (n % 3, n % 5) {
        (0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",
        (0, _) => "fizz",
        (_, 0) => "buzz",
        _ => {
            let s = n.to_string();
            Box::leak(s.into_boxed_str())
        }
    }
}

Gamanisi, last arm ondu &'static str return maaduttade, adu Box::leak function use maadi String inda create maadidadu. Ee function Box<T> na ownership tegedukondu adara contents ge pointer return maaduttade, effectively adannu leak maaduttade. Idu safe, yakendre return maadida pointer program na duration poorthi iruttade, aadare idannu care inda use maadabeku, yakendre idu automatically clean up aaguvudilla.

response_en:
Merge sort is a divide and conquer algorithm that works by recursively splitting the input array in half until the arrays are split into single elements. Then, the sorted arrays are merged back together in sorted order.

The key benefits of merge sort over a simpler algorithm like bubble sort are:

1. It is a stable sort that does not change the relative order of elements with equal keys.
2. It has an efficiency of O(n log n) time complexity, making it a relatively efficient algorithm even for large input sizes. Bubble sort, on the other hand, has a quadratic time complexity of O(n^2), making it very inefficient for larger inputs.
3. It is a generic algorithm that can sort any type of data for which a comparison function exists.

Here is a Rust implementation example:
```rust
fn merge_sort(vec: &mut [i32]) {
    if vec.len() < 2 {
        return;
    }

    let mid = vec.len() / 2;
    let (left, right) = vec.split_at_mut(mid);

    merge_sort(left);
    merge_sort(right);

    merge(left, right, vec);
}

fn merge(left: &mut [i32], right: &mut [i32], vec: &mut [i32]) {
    let mut i = 0;
    let mut j = 0;
    let mut k = 0;

    while i < left.len() && j < right.len() {
        if left[i] < right[j] {
            vec[k] = left[i];
            i += 1;
        } else {
            vec[k] = right[j];
            j += 1;
        }
        k += 1;
    }

    while i < left.len() {
        vec[k] = left[i];
        i += 1;
        k += 1;
    }

    while j < right.len() {
        vec[k] = right[j];
        j += 1;
        k += 1;
    }
}
```

romanized_response:
merge sort ondu divide and conquer algorithm. idu input array annu recursively half half aagi split madutta hogutte, arrays single elements aagi split aaguvavarege. nantara, sorted arrays annu sorted order nalli matte merge madalagutte.

bubble sort thara simpler algorithm ge compare madidare merge sort na key benefits ivu:

1. idu stable sort, andre equal keys iruva elements na relative order annu change madalla.
2. idara efficiency O(n log n) time complexity, adarinda large input sizes ge kooda idu relatively efficient algorithm. innondu kade bubble sort ge O(n^2) quadratic time complexity ide, adarinda larger inputs ge adu tumba inefficient.
3. idu generic algorithm, comparison function iruva yava type data annadaru sort madabahudu.

